## ACTIVE TASK

### D6.1–D6.5 Authenticated Mobile Shell & Home

- Branch `feat/d6-mobile-auth-shell-home`, based on `72aeff8`, which was still
  `origin/main` at VERIFY time: no divergence, no rebase or merge was needed. No
  migration, no schema/RLS/Storage change, no production write, no external
  provider call.
- The BUILD audit found: header, bottom-nav and Home already existed; the real
  gaps were
  four. The header had no avatar and put the search lens where the third action
  belongs; the mobile bar had `Account` and no `Cantina`; there was no avatar
  fallback below the initials; the Home hero printed the bare username.
- Reused, not rebuilt: `useVinea()` (`authProfilo.avatarUrl`, `authProfilo.userId`,
  `authProfileName`) as the auth/profile source of truth; `avatarSicuro()` /
  `percorsoAvatarPersonale()` / `riferimentoAvatarSicuro()` from the CLOSED
  avatar foundation; `HeaderInboxActions` for Messaggi + Notifiche; the existing
  `/messaggi`, `/notifiche`, `/account`, `/cantina`, `/esplora`, `/vendi`,
  `/community`, `/home` routes. No second shell, no new Home, no new Account
  route, no duplicated resolver or storage helper.
- New `src/lib/shell/navigazione-mobile.ts`: the two bar models plus
  `voceNavAttiva()` and `classiRicercaHeader()`. Authenticated bar is exactly
  Home (`/home`) / Ricerca / Vendi / Club / Cantina; the guest bar is unchanged
  and keeps `Account`. Extracting the model is what makes the shell verifiable
  without mounting React, which is this suite's existing convention.
- Fixed while there: the mobile bar used a bare `startsWith`, so `/vendite` — a
  real route — lit up `Vendi`. Now it matches on the `/` boundary, as the
  desktop bar already did.
- New `src/components/vinea/AvatarPersona.tsx`: priority foto → preset →
  silhouette, with `SilhouettePersona` exported separately so the fallback is
  not header-only. The silhouette is an inline SVG, so the bottom of the chain
  is never itself a network request. Initials are no longer the final fallback;
  `inizialiDa()` stays for `/account`, which was not touched.
- New `risolviAvatarPersona()` in `src/lib/profilo/avatar.ts` returns a
  discriminated `fonte`. It fails closed onto the silhouette for an absent
  value, a foreign user's folder, an off-catalogue preset, an external URL, and
  a photo whose Storage base is unusable — so no broken image and no invalid
  `src` can be emitted.
- Measured and worth recording: foto and preset can never both apply, because
  `profiles.avatar_url` is one column and the two shapes are disjoint
  (`/avatar/*.svg` vs `<uuid>/<uuid>.webp`). The stated priority is therefore
  explicit in code and observable through `fonte`, but cannot be violated at
  runtime. That mutual exclusivity is pinned by its own test.
- Header authenticated mobile: Messaggi, Notifiche, avatar, in that order, with
  the avatar last in the left-to-right actions row and therefore at the far
  right. The lens is `hidden md:inline-flex` when authenticated and keeps its
  exact previous classes when guest. The avatar is `md:hidden`, so the desktop
  shell — which already carries an `Account` link — is untouched.
- Home authenticated hero now reads `Bentornato, {nome}` from
  `authProfileName`. Loading, `AccessRequired` and `ProfileMissing` states, the
  hero visual language, the KPI row and the Cantina access are unchanged. No
  dashboard, no seller statistics, no Balance.
- The independent VERIFY audit read the real working tree, including the two
  untracked files `git diff` does not show until staged, and found three defects
  the BUILD report did not list. All three are corrected on the branch:
  1. the new avatar link set `aria-current` from a bare
     `pathname.startsWith("/account")` — the same defect class D6 had just
     removed from the bar. No `/account`-prefixed sibling route exists today, so
     it was latent, not observable. `percorsoAttivo()` is now the exported form
     of the `/`-boundary comparison, `voceNavAttiva()` is written on top of it,
     and the avatar uses it too;
  2. no test proved the shell actually branches on the role: replacing
     `navMobile(autenticato)` with a fixed list passed the whole suite. That is
     coverage the task required. Three assertions now pin the wiring, including
     that neither bar constant is named inside the component;
  3. `expect(azioni.indexOf("</div>", posAvatar)).toBeGreaterThan(posAvatar)`
     was vacuous — any later `</div>` satisfied it. The tail after the avatar is
     now delimited and asserted empty.
- Test-shape decision, measured rather than assumed: the suite is 51 files, all
  `.ts`, with no DOM library, no `bunfig.toml` preload and no rendering test.
  React-level assertions are therefore not available without adding a dependency
  and moving the lockfile, which is out of scope. Behaviour that can be pure
