### Phase 7g payout scheduler — shipped, historical

- Phase 7g payout scheduler readiness gate, shipped as PR #82, squash-merged to
  `e14daed`. All three CI jobs passed on head `a46cd2a`; Supabase Preview
  skipped because the PR carries no migration. No migration, Supabase write,
  Stripe call or secret/variable change was performed.
- Post-merge smoke executed once on `main`, run `32833173688`,
  `workflow_dispatch` on `e14daed`: **SUCCESS**, with the annotation
  `PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED non vale "true": nessuna invocazione, nessun
  payout.` and the marker `[payouts-release] disabilitato: scheduler non
  autorizzato`. No HTTP request, no payout, no `Configurazione mancante`, no
  error line; every secret slot was empty, so none was needed or exposed. The
  contrast is recorded: the last scheduled run before the merge, `32817376374`
  on `b52dd06`, failed with `Configurazione mancante: SUPABASE_URL`.
- The enabled branch was deliberately not exercised against production.
- Added the fail-closed repository gate `PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`, read by
  `.github/scripts/payouts-release-job.mjs` before any configuration lookup or
  HTTP call and passed in by `.github/workflows/payouts-auto-release.yml` as
  `vars.PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`.
- Absent, empty or any value other than the exact string `true`: no secret is
  read, no request is issued, no payout occurs, and the run ends successfully
  with the notice `Payouts scheduler disabilitato` and the marker
  `[payouts-release] disabilitato`. Exactly `true`: the pre-existing path runs
  unchanged and missing configuration, non-2xx HTTP, unexpected payload,
  timeout, `falliti > 0` and the >24h backlog all remain failures.
- The two gates stay independent: `PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED` authorizes the
  runner to call the function, `PAYMENTS_ENABLED` authorizes the real payout.
  Neither was enabled; the remote variable was not set.
- Remote state read during this task, by name only and without exposing values:
  the repository has **no** Actions variables and **no** Actions secrets. So
  `PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED` is absent and the shipped gate is closed, and the
  historical six-hourly failures are explained: `SUPABASE_URL`,
  `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` and `PAYOUTS_JOB_TOKEN` never existed.
- `payout_prepara`, `payout_coda`, `ordine_auto_rilascio_esegui`,
  `payout_registra_esito`, the Stripe transfer logic and the order state machine
  are untouched. The runner still sends only anon key, job token and batch; no
  service role reaches GitHub Actions.
- Targeted verification: `node --test .github/scripts/payouts-release-job.test.mjs`
  gives **15 passed / 0 failed**. Two control runs proved the new assertions
  bite: loosening the comparison to case-insensitive/trimmed fails 1 test,
  removing the gate fails 5. `git diff --check` is clean. The workflow YAML was
  parsed with the `js-yaml` already present in `frontend/node_modules`, without
  installing anything: the gate reaches the step as
  `vars.PAYOUTS_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`, there is no job- or step-level `if:`, and
